# Build output. `make build` puts everything here, so one entry covers every
# tool that will ever exist — including ones not written yet.
/bin/

# `go build ./...` from the repo root drops binaries beside the source instead.
# These named entries are a backstop for that; the CI guard in test.yml is the
# real safety net, because an allowlist of names fails OPEN — a compiled binary
# once reached the public module zip because /ratchet was listed and /lens was
# not, and module zips are immutable.
/ratchet
/strata
/lens
/docket

# Coverage output
cover.out
*.out
